       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for adults is 3200 mg/day under physician supervision, and OTC use is capped at 1200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this level:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. These risks rise sharply above the labeled limits, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily** (1200\u20132400 mg/day), a common dose for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg/day total** (for example, 400 mg four times daily).\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and include the clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
