       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A family visit and evening rounds aren't clinical reasons for 6400 mg/day of ibuprofen, which is twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1600 mg/day).\n\nIf the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can also enter a multimodal regimen. For example, scheduled acetaminophen up to 1000 mg every 8 hours could go alongside ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n\nIf there is a specific clinical indication that calls for 1600 mg per dose, please take it up with pharmacy or a clinical pharmacist. They can review it and, if it's justified, enter it through the appropriate channel. Tell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
